adjudication.rationale:
In the new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, decryption and JSON parsing are done without any error handling:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

If `symmetricDecrypt(...)` throws (e.g., tampered ciphertext, missing/invalid key) or returns a non-JSON string, `JSON.parse(...)` will throw. There is no `try/catch` around this (and `appCredentialWebhookRequestBodySchema.parse(req.body)` also throws on invalid bodies), so these failures will bubble up and result in an unhandled exception / 500 response rather than a controlled 400-style client error. This is directly verifiable from the diff.
